{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/574208-are-harmony-shifts-in-character-knowledge","id":574208,"title":"Are Harmony Shifts In-Character Knowledge?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-30T12:40:37-07:00","id":574208,"title":"Are Harmony Shifts In-Character Knowledge?","content":"I'm playing a ghost-wolf lost-cub type werewolf in an otherwise mostly-human game. For the fun of it, I started him out with Harmony 10 and Moon as his Passive Trigger. In the course of play, he ended up losing a dot of Harmony, and it led to an interesting discussion that I thought I'd probe the forum for opinions on.<br /> <br /> Would the character himself be aware that his Harmony had shifted? Would he know that the rising full moon won't force him to Change anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T12:51:46-07:00","id":574236,"title":"","content":"He would certainly notice the passive not triggering like it did before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T12:56:20-07:00","id":574240,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's an official answer in the book about this.<br /> <br /> Basically, while I feel that they'd know they had changed, they wouldn't necessarily know what happened. There's a lot of things you can notice as your Harmony goes up and down, but if you aren't told about it or experience it before, I see no reason why you should be naturally informed of it.<br /> <br /> Say a character has already raged during the past two full moons, but now they've experienced a Harmony shift and it's a common trigger, not passive. They might feel a nagging tingle urging them to look for the moon, where before they felt a rising surge of energy simply due to it rising into the sky. Then obviously once they don't rage at the moon being in that auspice, they might realize what's changed. There's some other things that shift, too, like shifting flows differently, and at the extremes you find it easier to move one way through the Gauntlet, which I might describe as feeling more 'anchored' and at ease when you're in the flesh or spirit world, depending on where the Harmony was at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T14:43:19-07:00","id":574379,"title":"","content":"I think in this specific case, the character would only be able to figure out that anything had changed if he was inside during his Auspice Moon and didn't rage. At that point, it would be obvious that something had changed, but without other Uratha to contextualize it for him, he wouldn't know why. If he had a pack to ease him into things, they could explain to him that he is part spirit and part flesh, and that when those two aspects of himself are out of balance, it makes him more susceptible to Kuruth. But as a lone, lost ghost wolf, he lacks a source for that kind of knowledge. He'll have to figure out what's changed on his own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T16:55:51-07:00","id":574480,"title":"","content":"I would say that its well known inside of Uratha culture, likely codified as part of the Moon Code. A lone wolf without guidance? I'd say he'd be guessing. He'd figure out something changed, but it'd be a guess to figure out what did it. Over time, he could work it out, I'd say<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T02:49:38-07:00","id":576250,"title":"","content":"10 to 9 is a bit hard to tell the difference with, unless he somehow falls through a locus. If he drops to 8 he'll get a much more obvious clue the first time he shifts and his clothes come with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}